            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "In my workflow using the new dir-listing, sticky definitely feels wrong.\nNon-sticky for me means least-surprising:\n- In a listing buffer mentally I know cwd is pinned to the listed dir, so I can fire `:!` confidently without bothering the % prefix.\n- In a normal file buffer, :find/:e etc. operate against the CWD I expect — not whatever buffer I happened to open it from.\n",
