            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> true, but the sticky behavior for buf-local dir will be \"different\" no matter what. there is no way for it to be consistent with win/tab behavior, even if we decide to make it sticky. because buffers can live in multiple windows, unlike windows/tabs.\n\nNot 100% confident in my understanding, but my initial idea of the consistent sticky behavior is something like this:\n- When creating a new tabpage it inherits the local directory of the current tabpage (if set).\n- When creating a new window it inherits the local directory of the current window (if set).\n- When creating a new buffer it inherits the local directory of the current buffer (if set).\n\nIt might indeed bring more breaking behavior for plugins in case buffer-local cwd is set At least this is more consistent and indicates that setting a buffer-local cwd should be done very intentionally and for a good reason.\n\n> > will lead to very subtle issues\n> \n> if you notice anything please comment here, that will help us decide what to do.\n\nWill do. However, I doubt any issue will become apparent before 0.13 release (after which users/plugins might start to use it). Which is a bit late.",
