            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I personally am a proponent of disabling \"stickiness\" for everything - tabpages, windows and buffers, and making it all opt-in.\n\nyou can achieve that via `:lcd!` / `:tcd!` (with \"!\") since https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41194\n\n\nanyway, after working on this for awhile, I see the logic in win/tab-local sticky. and yet I also see the logic in non-sticky buf-local dir.\n\nso far, no one has addressed the \"cons\" I listed for sticky `:bcd`, and the only argument in favor has been \"consistency\" (which as I mentioned, is not fully achievable).\n\ni'm generally a big proponent of consistency, but in this case, concrete examples are very much needed. i.e., actual examples of where the \"inconsistency\" is causing a concrete problem, and what behavior you expect instead.",
            "created_at": "2026-08-08T17:14:22Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41210#issuecomment-5227213719",
            "id": 5227213719,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/41210",
